  "worked_solution": "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t-1)+{cos}^{2}\u2061t & ={sin}^{2}\u2061t-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t+{cos}^{2}\u2061t \\\\  & =({sin}^{2}\u2061t+{cos}^{2}\u2061t)-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}\u2061t+{sin}^{2}\u2061t=1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t-1)+{cos}^{2}\u2061t=1-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t.\n$$",
